<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan State Oil gains 1.27 percent.</title>
<headline>Pakistan State Oil gains 1.27 percent.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan State Oil rose 3.50 rupees or 1.27 percent to 279 rupees on Thursday on news that the Karachi Electric Supply Corporation will pay back its dues to the firm, dealers said.</p>
<p>Dealers said the state-run KESC owes the state-run blue chip PSO two billion rupees for the purchase of furnace oil but will soon return one billion rupees to PSO by taking a one year loan from ABN Amro and ANZ Grindlays Banks at 18.1 percent per annum.</p>
</text>
